## A library's own AssemblyRefs against the program's references
## (ImplementationPlan.md M22.c item 7; 5.11.9's M22 texts; recon
## p2/bcl-binding.md 5.9 and p2/exports-multiasm.md 5.4 step 5): each
## AssemblyRef of a linked library that names no library of this link is
## compared with the references, or without references with the built-in
## table's mscorlib 4.0.0.0:
## - a newer version than the reference's is the error
##   '<library> references <name> <version>, newer than the reference <version>';
##   an older or equal one is fine;
## - a name the references do not have is the warning
##   '<library> references <name>, which is not among the references';
## - an AssemblyRef that names another library of the link is not checked.
## The references are Inputs/fakepack's (M21): pack holds FakeCore 8.0.0.0,
## FakeInterop 8.0.0.0 and FakeThreading 8.1.2.3, pack9 the same with
## FakeInterop 9.0.0.0, packnt pack without FakeThreading, mscorlib the
## one-file mscorlib 4.0.0.0. lib.o binds Marshal (FakeInterop) for its data
## and Interlocked (FakeThreading) for a fence; libb.o calls lib's bump.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj lib.ll -o lib.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj libb.ll -o libb.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj prog.ll -o prog.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj progb.ll -o progb.o
# RUN: mkdir pack pack9 packnt mscorlib v8 v9 none b out
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o pack/FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInterop.yaml -o pack/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeThreading.yaml -o pack/FakeThreading.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o pack9/FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInteropV9.yaml -o pack9/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeThreading.yaml -o pack9/FakeThreading.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o packnt/FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInterop.yaml -o packnt/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeMscorlib.yaml -o mscorlib/mscorlib.dll

# DEFINE: %{fc} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"

## The libraries: against pack9, pack, and no references.
# RUN: msil-ld -shared lib.o --reference=pack9 -o v9/lib.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: msil-ld -shared lib.o --reference=pack -o v8/lib.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: msil-ld -shared lib.o -o none/lib.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump v9/lib.dll | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V9-REFS
# V9-REFS:      {{^}}assemblyref 'FakeCore' ver 8.0.0.0 flags=0x00000000 key=B0 3F 5F 7F 11 D5 0A 3A culture=''{{$}}
# V9-REFS-NEXT: {{^}}assemblyref 'FakeInterop' ver 9.0.0.0 flags=0x00000000 key=B0 3F 5F 7F 11 D5 0A 3A culture=''{{$}}
# V9-REFS-NEXT: {{^}}assemblyref 'FakeThreading' ver 8.1.2.3 flags=0x00000000 key=31 BF 38 56 AD 36 4E 35 culture=''{{$}}

